  "title": "The $5 That Makes You Happier (Not on You) #shorts",
  "description": "Who's getting your coffee? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who always pays. Payday: Lila buys herself fancy headphones, and the buzz fades fast. In 'Spending Money on Others Promotes Happiness' (Science, 2008), Elizabeth Dunn, Lara Aknin and Michael Norton gave people a $5 or $20 bill to spend by 5 p.m. that day, either on themselves or on someone else. Those who spent it on others reported feeling happier at the end of the day; even $5 was enough. Psychologists call it prosocial spending. Treat someone. #psychology #shorts #happiness #money #kindness",
